================================================================================
PART A  free field: what p^4 content does Bianchi have?
================================================================================
A1  max |k_[lam F_{mu nu]}| over 4000 random (k, A_T):  4.885e-15
A2  sum_lam |k_lam F_{mu nu}|^2 / |k.F|^2 :  2.000000000000 .. 2.000000000000  (spread 4.4e-15)
    Weitzenboeck with Bianchi:  |grad F|^2 = |dF|^2 + |d*F|^2 = |D.F|^2
    and |D.F|^2 = (k^2)^2 |A_T|^2 : ONE invariant, direction-free, ZERO on the
    free EOM  k.F = 0.  So Bianchi's positive p^4 = the EOM square, nothing else.
A3  'Bianchi square' operator  sum |k_[lam F_{mu nu]}|^2 == 0 : p^4 coefficient
    is EXACTLY ZERO (not 'positive').  Same on the lattice: prod_{p in dc} U_p = 1.

